Synopsys Synthesis
==================

This directory contains the following sub-directories:

1. work       - contains the intermediate files produced by the Synopsys
                'analyze' command.
2. db         - contains the synthesised blocks in Synopsys .db format.
3. cell_lib   - this needs to contain a link or copy of the cell library.db
4. log        - contains log files of the commands run during synthesis
                for each block.
5. netlist    - contains the synthesised netlist of each block.
6. scr_common - contains Synopsys scripts which are common to other designs.
7. scr_sdram  - contains Synopsys scripts which are specific to the
                SDRAMC design.
8. report     - contains reports written out from synopsys. 
9. scr_scan   - contains Synopsys scripst which are specific to the scan
                insertion and ATPG.

Before synthesising the block, scripts will need to be modified to select
the required cell library and define directory paths:

1. The setup script, setup.scr in the sub-directory ./scr_common, needs
   modifying for
     - the cell library to target for synthesis
     - library cells not to be used for synthesis
     - location of the Synopsys read and write cache

   Refer to comments in the setup.scr script file for other
   parameters that might need to be modified.

2. The global script, global.scr in ./scr_common needs modifying for
     - worst and best case conditions of the cell library
     - default cell drive and load strength

3. The master compile script - sdram.cmd - is present in the 
   ./scr_sdram directory.  

   These contain the variable 'hdl' to select the hdl source being compiled.

   The path for design_root is specified using the environment variable
   $PERIPH. This requires build_sdram to be executed and sourcing SourceMe
   in the directory level above. Alternatively enter a fixed path.

4. The timing parameters for the AMBA AHB interface are defined by
   ahb_params.scr and the constraints set in ahb_slave.scr in ./scr_common.

5. The scan insertion script, sdram_scan.cmd
   script present in the ./scr_scan directory.

To synthesise the block, a control script - syn_sdram - is provided in
the scr_sdram directory. Please read the comments in the syn_sdram
file before starting the synthesis run.
 
To perform scan insertion the same control script syn_sdram in scr_sdram
directory can be used.
 
After the options are set in the syn_sdram file, start the synthesis using
the following command, from the ./scr_sdram directory.
 
syn_sdram <CR>

